{"schema_version":3,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:19-6","provision":"BCO 19-6","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"19-6","title":"Section 19-6","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/19-6/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/19-6","current_text":{"html":"<p>The license to preach the Gospel shall expire at the end of four years. The Presbytery may, if it thinks proper, renew it without further examination. The licentiate must apply for renewal prior to expiration. If the license expires, the stated clerk shall report the expiration to the Presbytery and to the individual's Session, and such action shall be recorded in the minutes. The procedures of <i>BCO</i> 19-2 must be followed for re-licensure and such fact shall be recorded in the minutes. The license may be terminated at any time by a simple majority vote of the issuing Presbytery. The Presbytery shall always record its reasons for this action in its minutes. <b>B. Internship</b></p>","text":"The license to preach the Gospel shall expire at the end of four years. The Presbytery may, if it thinks proper, renew it without further examination. The licentiate must apply for renewal prior to expiration. If the license expires, the stated clerk shall report the expiration to the Presbytery and to the individual's Session, and such action shall be recorded in the minutes. The procedures of BCO 19-2 must be followed for re-licensure and such fact shall be recorded in the minutes. The license may be terminated at any time by a simple majority vote of the issuing Presbytery. The Presbytery shall always record its reasons for this action in its minutes. B. Internship"},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"edce8a8dcd9ced63bb585bf922e6a97319ef62e1","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"128cf7cdd1263685b0a4c3f3f98d6149b2d89fd2b9b08848b1b45bbc05a5836d","assessment_fingerprint":"517b100d2e9006e313ab6d84d4f0f31593b77832f395383ba2227779470cd034","assessment_summary":{"status":"stale","file":"index/provision_link_adjudications.jsonl","total":11481,"expected":11481,"applied":0,"stale":11481,"unmatched":0,"unassessed":11481},"parent_id":"bco:19","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Recommendation and study papers are not comprehensively indexed by provision."},"history":"partial"},"relationship_count":11,"relationships":[{"id":"bco:19-6--case:cases/ga46_2018__2016-11.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga46_2018__2016-11.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Frazier v. Nashville Presbytery","year":2018,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga46_2018__2016-11.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga46_2018__2016-11.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:19-6--case:cases/ga46_2018__2016-11.md:occ-b7d24e6d8bb3","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga46_2018__2016-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga46_2018__2016-11.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga46_2018__2016-11.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["same-sex attraction","homosexuality","BCO 31-2 investigation","strong presumption of guilt","due diligence","great discretion","committee on judicial business","recusal","appearance of impropriety","indictment","complaint denied","standards of review","BCO 39-3.3 deference"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2016-11"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"The SJC denied a complaint challenging Nashville Presbytery's decision not to indict a teaching elder for allegedly sinful teaching on homosexuality and same-sex attraction. The adopted judgment held that the 147-page record showed Presbytery fulfilled its BCO 31-2 investigatory duty and did not show it erred in judgment when it declined process; the complaint was denied 20-0-1. Concurring opinions raised concerns about committee recusal, record clarity, and exegetical uses of Scripture, but they were separate and did not alter the denial."}},{"id":"bco:19-6--case:cases/ga38_2010__2009-11.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga38_2010__2009-11.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Larry Edison et al. v. Southwest Florida Presbytery","year":2010,"disposition":"out_of_order","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga38_2010__2009-11.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga38_2010__2009-11.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:19-6--case:cases/ga38_2010__2009-11.md:occ-ac8317d4fb25","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga38_2010__2009-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga38_2010__2009-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":134},"excerpt":"BCO 19-6 makes it plain that no privilege is conferred in licensure","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga38_2010__2009-11.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2009-11"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Ministers complained that Southwest Florida Presbytery improperly reexamined Bryan Gregory and reversed his examination, membership, and call after previously receiving him. The SJC upheld Presbytery’s authority to hear and sustain the earlier complaint but sustained the present complaint on the remedial actions. Sustaining a complaint did not itself undo prior acts; once Presbytery had treated Gregory as a member, his membership rights could be removed only through disciplinary due process. The SJC annulled the reexamination and March 24 actions and directed Presbytery to consider appropriate remedies. Gregory’s theology was not before it."}},{"id":"bco:19-6--overture:ga24_1996:24","record_id":"overture:ga24_1996:24","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 19-6 Regarding Termination of Licensure","year":1996,"disposition":"Approved & ratified (1997)","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga24_1996.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga24_1996.md","evidence_basis":"title_subject_reference","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:19-6--overture:ga24_1996:24:occ-f18857ce6dae","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga24_1996.html#ga24-p54","repository_path":"markdown/ga24_1996.md#ga24-p54","locator":{"fragment":"ga24-p54","page":54},"excerpt":"Amend BCO 19-6 Regarding Termination of Licensure","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga24_1996.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"source":"OVERTURE 24 From Ascension Presbytery (to B&O & CCB)"}},{"id":"bco:19-6--overture:ga15_1987:30","record_id":"overture:ga15_1987:30","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 19-6 to Drop Unlicensed Candidates from Presbytery Rolls","year":1987,"disposition":"Approved & ratified (1988)","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga15_1987.html","raw_url":"https://raw.g